  "texts": {
    "preamble": "Ravindra Singh Son Of Daljeet Singh vs State Of Rajasthan on 19 January, 2022",
    "facts": "The instant miscellaneous petition has been preferred on behalf of the petitioner challenging the order dated 07.01.2021 passed by learned Additional Chief Judicial Magistrate, No. 2, Kota in Criminal Regular Case No. 4391/2016 titled as State v. Pankaj & Ors. for the offence under Sections 7/16 of the Prevention of Food Adulteration Act whereby the application filed by the petitioner for conversion of process has been rejected. As soon the accused-petitioner got to know about issuance of warrant of arrest, he through his counsel moved an application under Section 70(2) of Cr.P.C. for conversion of process which has been rejected vide order dated 07.01.2021 and thereafter, the revision petition has also been rejected. The petitioner is a 61 years old man. No service of any regular process was ever affected upon him.",
    "arguments": "",
